# Subscriptions & Boost

## Trials are real subscriptions
A user "on free trial" is an **active store subscriber** (Apple/Google manage it;
`periodType = TRIAL`). The stores do **not** allow charging before a trial ends, so
never build a "pay early / skip the trial" flow on the subscription product, and never
show "already subscribed" as a dead-end to a trial user.

## Boost is opt-in — never auto-boost plain posts
- **Submit Prayer** creates a normal post (`applyBoost: false`). Success copy is
  **"Posted"** (or **"Sent for review"** when moderation is required). Never say
  "boosted" for this path.
- **Boost this prayer** submits with `applyBoost: true`. Success copy is **"Posted and
  boosted"** (or pending variant). Server applies Boost only when `applyBoost` is true
  (immediately if approved, or on moderator approval via `posts.boost_requested`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — auto-boost every eligible subscriber post
if (postStatus === "approved") postForResponse = await applyAutoBoostIfEligible(post);
// ✅ GOOD — only when the author explicitly chose Boost
if (postStatus === "approved" && applyBoostRequested) {
  postForResponse = await applyBoostToPost(post, user);
}
```

## Boost eligibility
- **Paid (`premium`)** and **admins**: unlimited Boost.
- **Trial (`trial`)**: **one Boost** for the trial period (`users.trial_boost_used_at`,
  or a pending `posts.boost_requested`). After that, show
  `TRIAL_BOOST_EXHAUSTED_MESSAGE` — do not allow another Boost until they convert to paid.
- Mirrored modules — change both together:
  - Server: `artifacts/api-server/src/lib/boostEligibility.ts`
  - Client: `mobile/lib/serverSubscription.ts` (`userCanUseBoostNow`), `mobile/lib/boostTrial.ts`

`canUseBoost` in RevenueCat also requires a confirmed store entitlement (not the
optimistic post-purchase flag) and `userCanUseBoostNow(user)` from `/auth/me`.

## Tier mapping is the webhook's job
`subscriptionFromEvent` maps store events → `premium | trial | free`. Don't infer tiers
elsewhere; read `user.subscription`.

## Only EXPIRATION revokes access
Access ends when the paid/trial period actually lapses, NOT when the user cancels.
- `EXPIRATION` → `free` (the only revoking event).
- `CANCELLATION` / `BILLING_ISSUE` → **ignored** for tier changes (see prior rule).
